<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna `option guardarm` (default `auto`), P8 goto-quality: the
    ruleBlockIfNoExit arm tie-break by code layout, applied only in functions
    the per-function detector (p3_dataflow/kuna_unoptimized.rs) calls
    unoptimized.

    unget is gcc 11 -O0 (-fno-pic -fno-stack-protector -fcf-protection=none):
        struct buf { char *data; long len; long pos; };
        int unget(int c, struct buf *bp)
        {
          if (c == -1 || bp == 0 || bp->pos == 0)
            return -1;
          bp->data[DEC(bp->pos)] = c;
          return c;
        }
    (DEC is the C pre-decrement operator, which an XML comment cannot spell.)
    Its prologue stores both argument registers to the frame and the body
    reloads them from there, so it is unoptimized; both arms of the guard end
    in a return, and the earlier one in the layout is the source's clause.

    backup is gcc 11 -O2 of
        void backup(void)
        { if (width() > 1 && narrow == 0) point = prev(point); else point -= 1; }
    with width, prev, narrow and point linked in. It keeps a value in no
    frame slot and has no frame pointer, so it is not called unoptimized, and
    its layout (the else arm first) is the optimizer's, not the author's.

    Pass 1 (default auto): unget prints the source's flat guard (#1) and
    backup keeps the out-index arm order (#3). Pass 2 (option guardarm off):
    unget nests its body under the negated guard, the old output (#2).
    Pass 3 (option guardarm on): the layout also decides backup's tie and
    puts the else arm first (#4).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true"></bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x101000">0000000000000000</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="unget"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100060" name="backup"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1000b0" name="width"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1000c0" name="prev"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option truthycond on</com>
  <com>option returndup on</com>
  <com>lo fu unget</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu backup</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option guardarm off</com>
  <com>lo fu unget</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option guardarm on</com>
  <com>lo fu backup</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="GUARDAUTO #1: by default the unoptimized function's guard is flat with the return as its clause (pass 1)" min="1" max="1">^  if \(\(\(a0 == -1\) \|\| \(!a1\)\) \|\| \(!a1->field_0x10\)\)
^    return -1;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GUARDAUTO #2: with the option off the body is nested under the negated guard (pass 2)" min="1" max="1">^  if \(\(\(a0 != -1\) &amp;&amp; \(a1\)\) &amp;&amp; \(a1->field_0x10\)\) \{</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GUARDAUTO #3: by default the optimized function keeps the out-index arm order (pass 1)" min="1" max="1">^  if \(\(2 &lt;= \(int4\)width\(\)\) &amp;&amp; \(!dat_101004\)\) \{</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GUARDAUTO #4: with the option on the layout decides the optimized function too (pass 3)" min="1" max="1">^  if \(\(\(int4\)width\(\) &lt;= 1\) \|\| \(dat_101004\)\) \{</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
